  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN-Water 2015-2020 - UN-Water 2015-2018</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UN-Water 2015-2020</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">There is no single UN entity dedicated exclusively to water issues. Instead over 30 UN organizations carry out water and sanitation programmes separately. This reflects the fact that water issues run through all of the UNs main focus areas but also the fragmentation in the water sector.

UN-Water is the United Nations inter-agency coordination mechanism for all freshwater related matters, including sanitation. Building on a long history of coordination in the UN system, UN-Water was formalized in 2003 by the&#xa0;UN System Chief Executives Board for Coordination.&#xa0;It provides the platform to address the cross-cutting nature of water and maximize system-wide coordinated action and coherence.

UN-Waters role is to coordinate the work so that the UN family delivers as one in response to water related challenges.

UN Water is made up of Members&#xa0;and&#xa0;Partners with the purpose to support UN Member States to sustainably manage water and sanitation by:

1. Inform Policies

2. Monitor and Report

3. Inspire Action</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UN-Water (UNW) &#xe4;r en organisation f&#xf6;r samordning och informationsutbyte mellan 31 olika FN-organ, organisationer och program som arbetar med vattenresurser, dricksvatten och sanitet. Genom att st&#xf6;dja gemensamma insatser och skapa synergieffekter mellan ytterligare 36 icke-FN-organisationer skapas ett merv&#xe4;rde f&#xf6;r genomf&#xf6;rande av p&#xe5;g&#xe5;ende och  planerade FN-program  och projekt. Denna beredning avser ett st&#xf6;d till UN Water 2015-2020. Totalt avtalsbelopp med Sida f&#xf6;r perioden &#xe4;r 36 mn skr och hela strategin &#xe4;r p&#xe5; ca 28 mn USD (200 mn skr) inklusive andra givares fr&#xe4;mst Schweiz, men ocks&#xe5; FN organisationernas medfinansiering .

Avsteg fr&#xe5;n Sidas insatsregel har noterats vad g&#xe4;ller paragraf 2.8.11. Krav p&#xe5; revision och revisionsstandrard: Sverige har som medlem i FN deltagit i beslut om att acceptera  externa och interna revisionsprocesser utifr&#xe5;n gjord riskanalys, SingleAudit principle samt &#xa7; 2.8.7 Korruption om att Avtalet ska ange att samarbetsparten omedelbart ska informera Sida vid misstankar om eller f&#xf6;rekomst av korruption.

Schweiz (SDC) har f&#xf6;r avsikt att forts&#xe4;tta sitt st&#xf6;d g&#xf6;r en beredning senare i &#xe5;r och Sida har en regelbunden diskussion med dom, om framtida st&#xf6;d och delar dokument. Detta &#xe4;r anledningen till att Sidas bed&#xf6;mning skrivs p&#xe5; engelska.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UN-Water(UNW) is an inter-agency mechanism. UNW functions as a body   for coordinating and information sharing among 28 different UN        agencies, organisations and programmes working with issues related to water resources, drinking water &amp; sanit. By supporting joint efforts  and synergies between an additional 24 non-UN partners, added value   is made to implem. of ongoing and/or planned UN programs/projects.</narrative>
  </description>
